445 - I'm But a Stranger Here
 / 
Key: F
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 445
Topic: Early Advent - 

Verse 1:
[F]I’m but [C7]a[F]stranger here,
[Gm]Heav’n [F]is [C]my [F]home;
[F]Earth is [C7]a[F]desert drear,
[Gm]Heav’n [F]is [C]my [F]home.
[F]Dan[Bb]ger [F]and sorrow [C7]stand
Round [F]me [C7]on every [F]hand;
[Bb]Heav’n is my [F]Fatherland,
[Dm]Heav’n [Gm]is [C7]my [F]home.

Verse 2:
[F]What [C7]though the [F]tempest rage,
[Gm]Heav'n [F]is [C]my [F]home;
[F]Short [C7]is [F]my pilgrimage,
[Gm]Heav'n [F]is [C]my [F]home;
[F]And [Bb]time's [F]wild [C7]wintry blast
[F]Soon [C7]shall be [F]over past;
[Bb]I shall reach [F]home at last,
[Dm]Heav'n [Gm]is [C7]my [F]home.

Verse 3:
[F]There [C7]at my [F]Savior's side
[Gm]Heav'n [F]is [C]my [F]home;
[F]I [C7]shall [F]be glorified,
[Gm]Heav'n [F]is [C]my [F]home;
[F]There [Bb]are the [F]good [C7]and blest,
[F]Those I [C7]love most [F]and best;
[Bb]And there I, [F]too, shall rest,
[Dm]Heav'n [Gm]is [C7]my [F]home.
